From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:28:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Skip threads without a TEB, or that have exited, when
 allocating a TLS slot in every thread.

Loading a DLL with TLS gives the new slot to every running thread.  A
thread just created has no TEB the server knows of yet: that was an
ERR, though the thread sets up its TLS itself under the loader lock
once it starts (Word printed it now and then).  A thread that has
exited still answers with its TEB, which may be another thread's by
then; its data was set again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
index 3b71ddbdf17..ae0c4802181 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -1372,11 +1372,18 @@ static BOOL alloc_tls_slot( LDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY *mod )
 
         if (thread) NtClose( thread );
         thread = next;
-        if (NtQueryInformationThread( thread, ThreadBasicInformation, &tbi, sizeof(tbi), NULL ) || !tbi.TebBaseAddress)
+        if (NtQueryInformationThread( thread, ThreadBasicInformation, &tbi, sizeof(tbi), NULL ))
         {
             ERR( "NtQueryInformationThread failed.\n" );
             continue;
         }
+        /* A thread just created has no TEB the server knows of yet, and sets up its TLS itself under the loader
+         * lock once it starts; one that has exited needs none, and its TEB may be another thread's by now. */
+        if (!tbi.TebBaseAddress || tbi.ExitStatus != STATUS_PENDING)
+        {
+            TRACE( "skipping thread %p, teb %p, status %#lx\n", thread, tbi.TebBaseAddress, tbi.ExitStatus );
+            continue;
+        }
         teb = tbi.TebBaseAddress;
         if (!teb->ThreadLocalStoragePointer)
         {
